---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Contact Us — eDistrict UP Seva" description="Contact eDistrict UP Seva by email for guide corrections and suggestions. For help with your application, official eDistrict helpline numbers are listed on this page." path="/en/contact-us/" altPath="/contact-us/" updated="22 October 2026">
  <div class="content-col">
    <h1 class="page-title">Contact Us</h1>

    <section class="box">
      <h2>How to reach us</h2>
      <p>If you find an error, outdated information or a gap in any of our guides — or if you would like a guide on a service we have not covered yet — write to us:</p>
      <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@edistrictupseva.com">contact@edistrictupseva.com</a></p>
      <p>Please mention the name or link of the page you are writing about, so we can check it quickly. We read every suggestion, and where a correction is valid, we update the guide. We usually reply within 2–3 working days.</p>
      <div class="note">We can only help with matters related to our guides — explaining a process, correcting a page, or taking a topic suggestion.</div>

      <h3>What we cannot do</h3>
      <p>eDistrict UP Seva is an information guide, not a government office. That means we <strong>cannot check the status of your application, issue a certificate, or access your eSathi account in any way</strong>. For anything related to an actual application, please use the official channels listed below.</p>
      <div class="warn">Please note: we never ask for your login ID, password, OTP or Aadhaar number. Anyone who asks you for these — on any website or call — should be treated as suspicious. Do not share them, and report the incident to the official helpline.</div>

      <h3>Who to contact for what</h3>
      <table class="info">
        <tr>
          <th>Contact us (this website)</th>
          <td>Errors or corrections in a guide, unclear information, topic suggestions — <strong>contact@edistrictupseva.com</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Official support (eDistrict helpdesk)</th>
          <td>Application status, login or password problems, payment issues, or any certificate-related difficulty — helpline: <strong>0522-2304706</strong>, email: <strong>ceghelpdesk@gmail.com</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Chief Minister Helpline</th>
          <td>For delays or complaints about any government service — <strong>1076</strong> (toll-free)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Official portal</th>
          <td>To apply, check status and download certificates — <strong>edistrict.up.gov.in</strong> (citizen login: eSathi)</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
